Author: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 26 07:01:11 2026 +1000

    provider: a gateway key's chosen models and accounts follow a provider renamed (#3630)
    
    provider.Rename carried the routing groups and their rules, classifiers, fast
    and off lists and weights, the catalog files, StepFun's sign-in, the model
    preferences and the visible lists to the provider's new id, but a gateway
    key's model allow-list and per-key account selection are kept in
    caller-keys.json (internal/access), which nothing rewrote. After the rename a
    key held to "old/m1" listed a model no provider provides ("not currently
    provided"), and a request on the models it named was refused, though the
    provider itself still served them.
    
    Agent.RenameProvider — the path the editor's id field and `magpie provider
    set <id> id=<new>` take — now moves them with access.RenameProvider: an entry
    naming the provider by its old id keeps meaning the same model or account
    under the new one, another provider's entries and a group's stay as they are,
    and no list gains an entry.
    
    RED->GREEN: TestRenameMovesGatewayKeyModels (internal/agent) sets up the
    reporter's steps through Agent.RenameProvider — a provider "old", a gateway
    key allowed two of its models plus one of another provider's, a group, and
    one account — then renames it to "new". At 01468003 it failed with
    models [old/m1 old/* group/top other/m2] want [new/m1 new/* group/top
    other/m2], accounts [old/8254c329a9] want [new/8254c329a9], and the key no
    longer allowing what it listed; with this change it passes.
    
    Ran: go test -tags nogui ./internal/access ./internal/cli ./internal/agent
    (ok), gofmt -l on the changed files (empty), go vet ./...,
    GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go vet -tags nogui ./..., GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64
    go vet ./..., go build ./... and the linux nogui and windows builds — all ok.
    internal/provider is red at 01468003 too, on
    TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials: "fatal error: close of synctest
    channel from outside bubble", an environment red unrelated to this change.
    Not tried: clicking through the editor's model picker in a browser.

